experiment: slotdose
  SHORT RUN — 150000 ticks against a minimum of 450000. derived: §52's primary cleared 2 SE mostly because its CONTROL drifted
  negative -- 79% of the contrast at 900k -- and a label-destroyed arm
  should sit at zero. THE NEXT MOVE IS NOT ANOTHER ARM. The formant gap
  decomposes EXACTLY into a SLOT TERM (all a per-context bias table can
  produce) and an OBJECT RESIDUAL (which it cannot), so this measures the
  estimator on arms already built: instrumentation only, no new mechanism,
  no genome field, no core change. H is the UNEQUAL-DOSE ARTEFACT and its
  SIGN IS DERIVED: the untaught voice already sits 30% of the way toward
  /a/ (G = +0.4950 of 1.6417), so a 50/50 compromise LOWERS G and the
  more-written slot is pulled further -- predicting sign(dG) = -sign(d
  dose). The primary T-B is a PAIRED SIGN TEST, 26 of 36 (p = 0.0057), so
  it assumes no SD; T-A is a bookkeeping self-test on the PINNED arm, whose
  cells are diagonal and whose residual must be EXACTLY zero, and a T-A
  failure VOIDS the log. Same seed, shift, nuisance and order as wordruler,
  so the gap column must reproduce §52's. kRead: every branch prints
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.

  the question      §53. §52's pre-registered primary cleared 2 SE mostly
                    because its CONTROL went negative (79% of it at 900k).
                    Why did the control move? Measured, not re-run.
  the method        the formant gap splits EXACTLY into a SLOT TERM -- all a
                    per-context bias table can produce -- and an OBJECT
                    RESIDUAL, which it cannot. No new mechanism, no new genome
                    field, no core change: instrumentation only.
  the hypothesis    UNEQUAL DOSE. The untaught voice already sits 30% of the
                    way toward /a/ (G = +0.4950 of 1.6417), so a 50/50
                    compromise LOWERS G -- and the more-written slot is pulled
                    further. Predicts sign(dG) = -sign(d dose). SIGN DERIVED.
  session           150.0 s of simulated life x 120 sessions, 4 arms
  instrument        slotdose   trial seed 0000000001357469   120 sessions
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

  CLAUSE 0 -- LIVENESS AND IDENTIFICATION, read on EVERY arm including the
  one whose null is load-bearing. A creature with != 2 live slots is DROPPED
  from the cell columns; the residual needs all four cells populated.
    T1.RET       n 36/36  dropped 0  present 1.0000  occ 0.6875  4-cell 30/36  median |d dose| 0.4599
    T1.RET.D     n 33/36  dropped 3  present 1.0000  occ 0.6847  4-cell 31/33  median |d dose| 0.3828
    T1.ORACLE.D  n 36/36  dropped 0  present 1.0000  occ 0.5000  4-cell 0/36  median |d dose| 0.0915
    T1.ORACLE    n 12/12  dropped 0  present 1.0000  occ 0.5000  4-cell 0/12  median |d dose| 0.1253

  THE MIXTURE -- H's PREMISE, TESTED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. Fraction of each
  slot's lessons that taught kWords[1] /i/. A DRAWN arm must read ~0.50 in
  BOTH slots (that is what makes it label-destroyed); a PAIRED arm must not.
    T1.RET       slot A 0.4693   slot B 0.5532   (paired)
    T1.RET.D     slot A 0.4917   slot B 0.4968   (drawn: both -> 0.50)
    T1.ORACLE.D  slot A 0.4825   slot B 0.5089   (drawn: both -> 0.50)
    T1.ORACLE    slot A 0.0000   slot B 1.0000   (paired)

  THE WORD PREFERENCE, G = perr(cube) - perr(ball), POSITIVE = NEARER /a/.
  `echo G` is the untaught reference measured in this run. Slot A is the one
  object 0 over-occupies, so sign(slot term) = sign(G_A - G_B) by construction.
    T1.RET       G_A +0.4785  G_B +0.5396  G_A-G_B -0.0610  mean G +0.4847  echo G +0.5021
    T1.RET.D     G_A +0.5131  G_B +0.6308  G_A-G_B -0.1178  mean G +0.5696  echo G +0.5117
    T1.ORACLE.D  G_A +0.5103  G_B +0.5531  G_A-G_B -0.0428  mean G +0.5322  echo G +0.5021
    T1.ORACLE    G_A +0.6296  G_B +0.4103  G_A-G_B +0.2192  mean G +0.5185  echo G +0.4896

  THE DECOMPOSITION. `gap` is §52's primary rebuilt from the cells and must
  reproduce the `pe` column beside it. `identity` is gap - (slot + residual)
  and is ARITHMETIC: anything but zero is a bookkeeping error of mine.
    T1.RET       gap -0.0002 +- 0.0073  (pe -0.0002)   SLOT -0.0019 +- 0.0059   RESIDUAL +0.0017   identity +2.78e-17
    T1.RET.D     gap -0.0080 +- 0.0052  (pe -0.0080)   SLOT -0.0116 +- 0.0054   RESIDUAL +0.0035   identity -2.78e-17
    T1.ORACLE.D  gap -0.0220 +- 0.0203  (pe -0.0220)   SLOT -0.0220 +- 0.0203   RESIDUAL +0.0000   identity +8.33e-17
    T1.ORACLE    gap +0.1049 +- 0.0312  (pe +0.1049)   SLOT +0.1049 +- 0.0312   RESIDUAL +0.0000   identity +5.55e-17

  T-A -- THE BOOKKEEPING SELF-TEST. A PINNED index makes the cells exactly
  diagonal, so T1.ORACLE's residual must be EXACTLY zero and its slot term
  must equal its gap. Worst identity over all 120 creatures +8.33e-17.
    identity zero everywhere  PASS
    ORACLE residual zero      PASS (+0.00e+00)

  T-B -- THE PRIMARY, A PAIRED SIGN TEST ON T1.RET.D. Per creature, does
  sign(G_A - G_B) OPPOSE sign(dose_A - dose_B)? Bar >=26 of 36 (p = 0.0057).
    T1.RET       oppose 18  agree 18  tied  0
    T1.RET.D     oppose 20  agree 13  tied  0
    T1.ORACLE.D  oppose 14  agree 22  tied  0
    T1.ORACLE    oppose  6  agree  6  tied  0

  T-C -- THE SHARE. How much of T1.RET.D's displacement the slot route
  accounts for, and the per-creature regression of gap on signed dose.
    slot term -0.0116 of gap -0.0080 = 144% of it
    slope d gap / d dose -0.0148 +- 0.0145 (-1.0 SE)   H predicts NEGATIVE

  THE VERDICT.

    (4b) NO VERDICT ON H: oppose 20, agree 13 of 33, neither at the bar of
